{"school":{"dbn":"31R009","name":"Naples Street Elementary School","boro":"Staten Island","district":"31","district_label":"District 31","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EC|EMS","school_type":"Elementary","grades":"PK-5","status":"open","enrollment":312,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"1055 Targee Street, Staten Island, NY 10304","phone":"718-876-4610","website":"WWW.PS9SI.ORG","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/kindergarten/64800","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"At PS 9, students, staff and families are encouraged to \u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009cBe a PS 9 STAR\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009d by using their VOICE. Through our core values of Vision, Opportunity, Independence, Collaboration, and Expression, our school community strives to use Safety, Teamwork, Actions, and Respect to reach their full potential.\n\nOne of the most promising instructional practices is empowering students, staff and families to be leaders in education. Students have many opportunities to have a voice and choice in their instruction. They can develop lesson plans, create resources, lead a small group, assess themselves and their peers, and reflect on their performance. Through this coaching model, students deepen and strengthen their content knowledge while developing their confidence and honing their leadership skills.\n\nTeachers are empowered to be leaders as well. Through extensive professional development opportunities, teachers deepen their content knowledge and are \u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009cleads\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009d for other teachers. Leads develop the units of study and lead the admin periods where they review the units, resources, and instructional practices that will be employed in the upcoming units. In addition, teachers welcome their colleagues into their classrooms to observe promising practices. \n\nLike staff and students, families are invited to be leaders in the school community. Through our committees and focus groups, we readily implement feedback and utilize the talents of our families to strengthen the relationship between home and school. Families have presented read alouds, shared cultural traditions, and explained their professions.\n\nAt PS 9 we are extremely proud of the culture of empowerment we have established where everyone can \u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009cBe a PS 9 STAR.\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u009d\n This school has ASD Nest: Open to students currently enrolled in the ASD (Autism Spectrum Disorder) Nest program. If you are applying to ASD programs for the first time, please visit www.schools.nyc.gov/specializedprograms for the application and contact ASDprograms@schools.nyc.gov with questions.","start_time":"8:00 AM","end_time":"2:20 PM","languages":"Albanian;Arabic;Chinese;Italian;Polish;Russian;Spanish","subway":null,"bus":"S53, S74, S76, S78, S84, S86, S93, SIM15, SIM33C, SIM35, SIM3C","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":null,"latitude":40.602594,"longitude":-74.090971,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":"2015-16","last_year":"2024-25"},"series":{"attendance_inperson_k8_all":{"y":["2020-21"],"v":[0.968],"st":["ok"],"n":[192.0]},"attendance_k8_all":{"y":["2018-19","2019-20","2020-21","2021-22","2022-23","2023-24","2024-25"],"v":[0.959,0.958,0.971,0.943,0.936,0.946,0.952],"s